s. Not enough.\n\nThus we need to find a pair of non-sunny lines covering at least 6 points, leaving at most 4 points that can be covered by 2 sunny lines. We tried many combos, but maybe there is a configuration that works.\n\nLet's systematically search for pairs of non-sunny lines (vertical/horizontal/diagonal) and see the leftover points. There are limited possibilities: vertical lines x=1,2,3,4; horizontal lines y=1,2,3,4; diagonal lines x+y=c for c=2,3,4,5 (since a+b ≤5). Let's list all possible non-sunny lines and the points they cover:\n\n- V1: (1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4) (4 points)\n- V2: (2,1),(2,2),(2,3) (3)\n- V3: (3,1),(3,2) (2)\n- V4: (4,1) (1)\n\n- H1: (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1) (4)\n- H2: (1,2),(2,2),(3,2) (3)\n- H3: (1,3),(2,3) (2)\n- H4: (1,4) (1)\n\n- D2 (x+y=2): (1,1) (1)\n- D3 (x+y=3): (1,2),(2,1) (2)\n- D4 (x+y=4): (1,3),(2,2),(3,1) (3)\n- D5 (x+y=5): (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1) (4)\n\nNow we need to pick two lines from this set (could be same type or different) that are distinct. Compute union size.\n\nWe can compute union sizes for each pair. Let's do manually.\n\nWe need union size at least 6 (so leftover ≤4). Let's compute union sizes for each pair.\n\nWe'll list pairs and union size.\n\nFirst, V1 (size 4) with each other:\n\n- V1 + V2: V1 ∪ V2 = points: V1 (1,1)-(1,4) plus V2 (2,1),(2,2),(2,3). No overlap. So union size = 4+3 = 7.\n\n- V1 + V3: V3 = (3,1),(3,2). No overlap with V1. Union size = 4+2 = 6.\n\n- V1 + V4: V4 = (4,1). No overlap. Union size = 4+1 = 5.\n\n- V1 + H1: H1 = (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). Overlap at (1,1). Union = V1 (4) + H1 (4) - 1 = 7.\n\n- V1 + H2: H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2). Overlap at (1,2). Union = 4+3-1 = 6.\n\n- V1 + H3: H3 = (1,3),(2,3). Overlap at (1,3). Union = 4+2-1 = 5.\n\n- V1 + H4: H4 = (1,4). Overlap at (1,4). Union = 4+1-1 = 4.\n\n- V1 + D2: D2 = (1,1). Overlap at (1,1). Union = 4+1-1 = 4.\n\n- V1 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). Overlap at (1,2). Union = 4+2-1 = 5.\n\n- V1 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (1,3). Union = 4+3-1 = 6.\n\n- V1 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (1,4). Union = 4+4-1 = 7.\n\nNow V2 (size 3) with others (excluding V1 already considered):\n\n- V2 + V3: V2 = (2,1),(2,2),(2,3); V3 = (3,1),(3,2). No overlap. Union size = 3+2 = 5.\n\n- V2 + V4: V4 = (4,1). No overlap. Union = 3+1 = 4.\n\n- V2 + H1: H1 = (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). Overlap at (2,1). Union = 3+4-1 = 6.\n\n- V2 + H2: H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2). Overlap at (2,2). Union = 3+3-1 = 5.\n\n- V2 + H3: H3 = (1,3),(2,3). Overlap at (2,3). Union = 3+2-1 = 4.\n\n- V2 + H4: H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 3+1 = 4.\n\n- V2 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 3+1 = 4.\n\n- V2 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). Overlap at (2,1). Union = 3+2-1 = 4.\n\n- V2 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (2,2). Union = 3+3-1 = 5.\n\n- V2 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (2,3). Union = 3+4-1 = 6.\n\nNow V3 (size 2) with others (excluding previous combos):\n\n- V3 + V4: V3 = (3,1),(3,2); V4 = (4,1). No overlap. Union = 2+1 = 3.\n\n- V3 + H1: H1 = (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). Overlap at (3,1). Union = 2+4-1 = 5.\n\n- V3 + H2: H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2). Overlap at (3,2). Union = 2+3-1 = 4.\n\n- V3 + H3: H3 = (1,3),(2,3). No overlap. Union = 2+2 = 4.\n\n- V3 + H4: H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 2+1 = 3.\n\n- V3 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 2+1 = 3.\n\n- V3 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). No overlap. Union = 2+2 = 4.\n\n- V3 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (3,1). Union = 2+3-1 = 4.\n\n- V3 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (3,2). Union = 2+4-1 = 5.\n\nNow V4 (size 1) with others (excluding previous combos):\n\n- V4 + H1: H1 = (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). Overlap at (4,1). Union = 1+4-1 = 4.\n\n- V4 + H2: H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2). No overlap. Union = 1+3 = 4.\n\n- V4 + H3: H3 = (1,3),(2,3). No overlap. Union = 1+2 = 3.\n\n- V4 + H4: H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 1+1 = 2.\n\n- V4 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 1+1 = 2.\n\n- V4 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). No overlap. Union = 1+2 = 3.\n\n- V4 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). No overlap. Union = 1+3 = 4.\n\n- V4 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (4,1). Union = 1+4-1 = 4.\n\nNow H1 (size 4) with others (excluding combos with V's already considered):\n\n- H1 + H2: H1 = (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1); H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2). No overlap. Union = 4+3 = 7.\n\n- H1 + H3: H3 = (1,3),(2,3). No overlap. Union = 4+2 = 6.\n\n- H1 + H4: H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 4+1 = 5.\n\n- H1 + D2: D2 = (1,1). Overlap at (1,1). Union = 4+1-1 = 4.\n\n- H1 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). Overlap at (2,1). Union = 4+2-1 = 5.\n\n- H1 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (3,1). Union = 4+3-1 = 6.\n\n- H1 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (4,1). Union = 4+4-1 = 7.\n\nNow H2 (size 3) with others (excluding combos with V's and H1 already considered):\n\n- H2 + H3: H2 = (1,2),(2,2),(3,2); H3 = (1,3),(2,3). No overlap. Union = 3+2 = 5.\n\n- H2 + H4: H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 3+1 = 4.\n\n- H2 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 3+1 = 4.\n\n- H2 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). Overlap at (1,2). Union = 3+2-1 = 4.\n\n- H2 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (2,2). Union = 3+3-1 = 5.\n\n- H2 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (3,2). Union = 3+4-1 = 6.\n\nNow H3 (size 2) with others (excluding combos with V's, H1, H2):\n\n- H3 + H4: H3 = (1,3),(2,3); H4 = (1,4). No overlap. Union = 2+1 = 3.\n\n- H3 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 2+1 = 3.\n\n- H3 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). No overlap. Union = 2+2 = 4.\n\n- H3 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). Overlap at (1,3). Union = 2+3-1 = 4.\n\n- H3 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (2,3). Union = 2+4-1 = 5.\n\nNow H4 (size 1) with others (excluding combos with V's, H1, H2, H3):\n\n- H4 + D2: D2 = (1,1). No overlap. Union = 1+1 = 2.\n\n- H4 + D3: D3 = (1,2),(2,1). No overlap. Union = 1+2 = 3.\n\n- H4 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). No overlap. Union = 1+3 = 4.\n\n- H4 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). Overlap at (1,4). Union = 1+4-1 = 4.\n\nNow D2 (size 1) with others (excluding combos with V's, H's, D3, D4, D5):\n\n- D2 + D3: D2 = (1,1); D3 = (1,2),(2,1). No overlap. Union = 1+2 = 3.\n\n- D2 + D4: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). No overlap. Union = 1+3 = 4.\n\n- D2 + D5: D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). No overlap. Union = 1+4 = 5.\n\nNow D3 (size 2) with D4, D5:\n\n- D3 + D4: D3 = (1,2),(2,1); D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1). No overlap. Union = 2+3 = 5.\n\n- D3 + D5: D3 = (1,2),(2,1); D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). No overlap. Union = 2+4 = 6.\n\nNow D4 (size 3) with D5:\n\n- D4 + D5: D4 = (1,3),(2,2),(3,1); D5 = (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1). No overlap. Union = 3+4 = 7.\n\nThus we have all possible pairs and union sizes.\n\nNow we need to consider each pair with union size >=6 (so leftover ≤4). For each such pair, we need to check if the leftover points can be covered by 2 sunny lines.\n\nList pairs with union size >=6:\n\n- V1+V2: union size 7, leftover 3 points: (3,1),(3,2),(4,1). Already considered, fails.\n\n- V1+V3: union size 6, leftover 4 points: (2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(4,1). Actually need to compute leftover for V1+V3. V1 = (1,1)-(1,4). V3 = (3,1),(3,2). Union = { (1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(3,1),(3,2) }. Leftover points: (2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(4,1). That's 4 points. Need to cover with 2 sunny lines. Let's see if possible.\n\nRemaining points: (2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(4,1). Check pairs: (2,1)-(2,2) vertical, not sunny. (2,1)-(2,3) vertical, not sunny. (2,1)-(4,1) horizontal, not sunny. (2,2)-(2,3) vertical, not sunny. (2,2)-(4,1) slope = (1-2)/(4-2) = -1/2, sunny. So we can pair (2,2) with (4,1) using a sunny line L1: slope -0.5. Then remaining points: (2,1),(2,3). They are vertical line x=2, not sunny. So we would need a sunny line covering both (2,1) and (2,3) but that's vertical, not allowed. So we need separate sunny lines for each, requiring 3 sunny lines. So fails.\n\n- V1+H1: union size 7, leftover points: (2,2),(2,3),(3,2). Actually union = V1 (1,1)-(1,4) plus H1 (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). Union = (1,1)-(1,4),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1). That's 7 points. Leftover: (2,2)